class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Enhances flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">ground cumin</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds depth to the spice mix</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">brown sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Balances the spice</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7181-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7181\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Lined with parchment paper</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 large bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing nuts and oil</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing spices</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7181-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7181-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7181\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Coating</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-1-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Toss mixed nuts with olive oil in a large bowl.</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Spice Mix</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-2-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Combine chili powder, smoked paprika, cayenne, garlic powder, cumin, salt, and brown sugar in a small bowl.</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Spicing</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-3-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Sprinkle the spice mix over the nuts and toss well.</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Baking</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-4-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Spread the nuts on a baking sheet and bake for 12–15 minutes, stirring halfway through.</span></div></li></ol></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Cooling</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7181-step-5-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Let the nuts cool completely before serving.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-7181-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><span style=\"display: block;\">give me a table with html code of nutrition for this recipe Revolutionary taste for spicy nuts really Jaw-dropping feast, ingredients:  </span><div class=\"wprm-spacer\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>mixed nuts (almonds, cashews, peanuts)</strong> – 2 cups</li>\n<li><strong>olive oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n<li><strong>chili powder</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>smoked paprika</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>cayenne pepper</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>garlic powder</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>ground cumin</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n<li><strong>brown sugar</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these delightful ingredients to create your own spicy <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nut_(food)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nuts</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Flavorful-Spicy-Nuts.webp\" alt=\"A colorful assortment of mixed nuts seasoned with spices on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-7179\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Flavorful-Spicy-Nuts.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Flavorful-Spicy-Nuts-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>mixed nuts (almonds, cashews, peanuts)</strong> – 2 cups</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>olive oil</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>chili powder</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>smoked paprika</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>cayenne pepper</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>garlic powder</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>ground cumin</strong> – 1/2 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>salt</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>brown sugar</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-spicy-nuts\"><strong>How to Make Spicy Nuts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready for a flavor explosion! This recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare and 12–15 minutes to cook. Let the nuts cool completely before diving in for the ultimate snacking experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Guide-to-Making-Spicy-Nuts.webp\" alt=\"Four-step process of making spicy nuts, including preheating the oven, coating nuts with olive oil, preparing a spice mix, and baking the nuts.\" class=\"wp-image-7180\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Guide-to-Making-Spicy-Nuts.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Guide-to-Making-Spicy-Nuts-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">First things first, preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). This will ensure your nuts get perfectly toasted.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Coat the Nuts</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a large bowl, toss your mixed nuts with a drizzle of olive oil. Make sure they are evenly coated for that delicious flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Prepare the Spice Mix</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, combine chili powder, smoked paprika, cayenne, garlic powder, cumin, salt, and brown sugar. This spice mix is where the magic happens!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Spice It Up</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sprinkle the spice mix over the coated nuts. Toss them well to ensure every nut is bursting with flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Bake the Nuts</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spread the spiced nuts in a single layer on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Bake for 12–15 minutes, stirring once halfway through, until they are fragrant and toasted.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Cool and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once baked, let the nuts cool completely before serving. Enjoy your spicy nuts as a snack or a party treat!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm and crunchy</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-spicy-nuts\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making spicy nuts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Experiment with different nuts for unique flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust spice levels to suit your taste preferences.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Toast nuts lightly before seasoning for enhanced crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the nuts cool completely before storing to maintain crispness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try adding a touch of maple syrup for a sweet-spicy twist.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-spicy-nuts\"><strong>How to Serve this spicy nuts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve as a crunchy snack during movie nights.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a refreshing cucumber and yogurt dip.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top your salads for an extra kick and crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix into trail mix for a spicy twist on a classic.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a topping for creamy soups for added texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include in a charcuterie board for a delightful surprise.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of hummus for a flavorful dip.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your spicy nuts fresh and tasty:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow spicy nuts to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep in a cool, dry place for up to two weeks.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For longer freshness, refrigerate.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Place cooled spicy nuts in a freezer-safe bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove as much air as possible before sealing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to three months.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Thaw in the fridge before using.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Spread nuts on a baking sheet in a single layer.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for about 5-10 minutes until warm.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy them fresh and crunchy!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Are spicy nuts good for you?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Spicy nuts can be a healthy snack option when consumed in moderation. They are packed with protein, healthy fats, and essential nutrients. The spices used can also have health benefits, such as boosting metabolism and providing antioxidants. Just be mindful of portion sizes, as nuts are calorie-dense!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How do you add spice to nuts?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Adding spice to nuts is simple and fun! You can toss them in a mixture of your favorite spices, such as cayenne pepper, chili powder, or smoked paprika, along with a bit of oil to help the spices stick. Roasting them in the oven enhances the flavors and gives them a delightful crunch. Experiment with different spice blends to find your perfect kick!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What is the spiciest nut in the world?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While there isn&#8217;t a definitive &#8216;spiciest nut,&#8217; many people consider the Carolina Reaper peanuts to be among the hottest. These peanuts are coated with Carolina Reaper pepper powder, known for its extreme heat. If you&#8217;re looking for a challenge, these spicy nuts will definitely deliver a fiery experience!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What is the unhealthiest nut to eat?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While all nuts have health benefits, some can be less healthy depending on how they are processed. For example, nuts that are heavily salted or coated in sugar can be less nutritious. Additionally, nuts fried in unhealthy oils can also be considered less healthy. Opt for raw or dry-roasted nuts for the best health benefits!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to indulge in a delightful crunch with these spicy nuts! They’re not just a snack; they’re a celebration of flavor that’s super easy to whip up. So gather your ingredients, let your taste buds dance, and enjoy this simple yet rewarding treat. Trust me, once you start, you won’t be able to stop!</p>\n",
